  "interpretation": "The first design (parallel 8 MiB ranged GETs) made W3 downloads slower in every round (median 146.8 -> 132.3 MiB/s). On the local stack per-request cost dominates and parallelism adds contention (raw reads above). The final default streams each piece with one ranged GET: W3 downloads at parity (+3.1, +2.3, -2.1 MiB/s) and W1 faster in every round (+12.1, +7.9, +6.9 MiB/s; median 152.7 -> 162.3). All uploads and downloads completed and verified. Parallel ranged reads remain available (download_prefetch > 1) for high-latency storage, to be measured on real S3 in Task 22."
